WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.860
HARRIS: Good evening.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.560
I'm Ellen Harris, Associate
Provost for the Arts,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.270
and it's my very
special pleasure

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:23.070
to welcome you tonight to this
showcase concert of MIT student

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.110
music-making.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.140
I want to take an opportunity
to point out to you,

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.470
to emphasize that, however
wonderful this concert is,

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.560
that it is only a fraction
of the music-making that goes

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:37.890
on at MIT, and I urge you--

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.800
after the concert,
not during the music

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.350
-to read the center portion
of your program, which

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.360
will give you some
more information

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:49.450
about the kind of music-making
that goes on here.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.570
And I'd like to say, beyond
that, that, of course,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.540
music-making is only a fraction
of the arts on this campus.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:59.130
We also have many programs
in the visual arts,

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:03.690
in theater, in dance, and in
writing, to name but a few.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.840
And we'll try to schedule
showcase concerts for all

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.040
of those things down the line.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.670
We'll let you know.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:13.140
Of course, it
wouldn't be a concert

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.420
if there weren't
an announcement.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.360
So let me make the announcement
for the evening, which

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.530
is that we are very sorry that
John Oliver, the conductor

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:25.770
of the chamber
choir, will not be

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.840
able to conduct
tonight because he has

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.990
a very painful fractured foot.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.230
We are happy, however,
to have William C.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:37.200
Cutter, the Assistant Conductor,
who will be conducting,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.940
not only tonight, but tomorrow
at the Inauguration, also.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.390
And we are very
lucky, and we are

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.720
very happy to have
Mr. Cutter with us.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.540
I would also like
to invite all of you

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.650
to come to the Student Center
following the concert--

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:57.480
to the third floor, where you
can meet the student performers

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.440
and composers whose work is
being highlighted tonight.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.380
They and I look forward
to greeting you there.

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:05.854
Thank you very much.

00:02:05.854 --> 00:02:10.210
[APPLAUSE]

